schema: "0.4"
id: npl-blueprint-12-admin-authz
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo (structured prompt-definition language + MCP agent toolchain) — Admin: Authz (MCP Keys + PBAC) screen.
# Theme tenets: cool drafting sheet, faint grid texture, thin cyan rules + monospace annotations, near-square 2px corners, one warm redline for markup.
# Palette: sheet #f5f8fc, navy ink #14263f, blueprint-blue #245ea8, drafting cyan #0e9bd6, redline #c05a3e.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    platform-administration surface for NoizuPromptLingo — a structured
    prompt-definition language and MCP agent toolchain. The register is a
    technical drafting sheet: cool, exacting, calm — "drawn by someone who
    measures twice." Structure is the aesthetic — a faint background grid, thin
    cyan rules, dimension lines, and monospace callout labels do the work.
    Engineered IBM Plex Sans for UI, IBM Plex Mono for every precise value.
    Near-square corners, nearly flat surfaces, no gradients or glow. The only
    warm color is a single red-oxide redline reserved for markup and attention.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the Authorization Control Center (Admin:
    Authz) of NoizuPromptLingo — a platform-admin screen combining PBAC policy
    simulation with MCP key-usage auditing.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (three bands): a slim LEFT ADMIN NAV RAIL that reads like a
    sheet index (thin cyan active left-rule, small mono section labels); a
    dominant CENTER work area of stacked title-block cards; the whole canvas
    backed by a faint, static blueprint grid (fine minor lines, heavier major
    lines, very low contrast).

    TOP STRIP: a monospace breadcrumb path "admin / authz" and a title
    "Authorization" in medium-weight sans, with a small mono coordinate readout
    at the far right like a drawing's title block.

    PBAC POLICY SIMULATOR (primary card, title-block header labeled "Policy
    Simulator"): three cyan-ruled input fields on the grid, each with a small
    monospace dimension-label above — "actor", "action", "resource" — showing
    sample values (a member handle, a tool action such as tools.call, a resource
    path). A blueprint-blue primary "Run check" button at the right. The result
    reads DENIED as a warm redline attention callout (a left redline rule + faint
    tint, the word set in ink).

    DENIAL EXPLANATION PANEL (auto-expanded beneath the simulator): a rule-trace
    as a vertical list joined by thin cyan rules — matched and unmatched policy
    rules with monospace policy identifiers, each row marked pass or fail, the
    deciding rule pulled out with a redline margin mark; dimension-line separators
    between rules.

    MCP KEY USAGE AUDIT TABLE (second card, title-block header "Key Usage"): a
    dense cross-org audit table with a cyan dimension-line beneath 500-weight sans
    column headers (Org, Key, Action, When, Result), monospace key-prefix and
    timestamp columns, quiet cool-hairline row separators, and a faint cyan
    row-hover tint. A row of filter chips above it (org, key, date range).

    SHADOW-MODE MISMATCH LOG (right-side panel, header "Shadow-mode mismatches"):
    a compact list of tool_guard identity mismatches recorded without enforcement
    — monospace identity pairs (expected vs presented), each flagged with a small
    redline markup and a muted "not enforced" note.

    PALETTE & TYPE: a pale cool drafting-sheet canvas carrying dark navy drafting
    ink. Structure is blueprint blue; thin rules and highlights are a drafting
    cyan; a single warm red-oxide redline is reserved for markup, denials, and
    attention — the red pencil on a blue drawing. Neutrals are cool-tinted toward
    blue, never warm, never pure gray. Engineered IBM Plex Sans for UI and body;
    IBM Plex Mono carries every precise value — policy identifiers, scope and
    resource paths, actor/action keys, timestamps, and the small callout labels
    above fields.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: near-square corners — drawn, not soft, not stamped. Borders
    are the drawing: thin single-pixel cyan and blueprint-blue rules form every
    cell divider, panel edge, and dimension line; surfaces are the paper between
    them. Nearly flat — cards rest on a rule and a faint tone step, never a drop
    shadow. The faint blueprint grid sits under the whole canvas, static and
    low-contrast — present when you look, gone when you read.

    MOOD: precise, technical, trustworthy within five seconds. Cool, exacting,
    calm — a configuration surface drawn on an engineer's drafting table where
    correctness and legibility of structure matter more than warmth.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Admin: Authz — PBAC policy simulator (actor/action/resource) with an auto-expanded denial explanation, an MCP key-usage audit table with filters, and a shadow-mode mismatch log"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Cool drafting sheet, faint blueprint grid, thin cyan/blueprint-blue rules, monospace values, near-square corners, single warm redline for markup — not generic UI defaults"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear visual hierarchy, plausible real-product admin layout with title-block cards"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"

tags: [npl-blueprint, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup]
